Description: Export the xdg_toplevel of a Wayland GdkWindow and signal its creation.
 Emits the xdg-toplevel-realized signal on a GdkWaylandWindow when its xdg_toplevel is created but before it is
 committed, and adds gdk_wayland_window_get_xdg_toplevel(). Firefox uses both for Wayland session restore, to name
 its windows to the compositor before they are mapped, and disables session restore when the signal is missing.
Author: Martin Stransky <stransky@redhat.com>
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/commit/edc9d508c3227d96de1e34aa3d5808a255f0e10b
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/merge_requests/9852
Applied-Upstream: gtk-3-24 branch after 3.24.52, not yet in a release
Last-Update: 2026-11-02
